{
"content_id": "133139",
"reference_id": 109193,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "1 Kings 9:1–9",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "11009001-11009009",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "None",
"content": "<p>God repeated to Solomon the covenant that he had made with David. He told Solomon to walk faithfully with him like David had done. This means that someone is to <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132301\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">love God</data> and obey him as long as they live.</p><p>David hadn’t obeyed all the <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132281\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">Law of Moses</data>. He did some things that God hated. Those events are recorded in 2 Samuel. But he always turned away from his sin, <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132292\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">repented</data> and trusted God to forgive him.</p><p>He always <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132278\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">worshipped only God</data> and never worshipped <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132230\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">false gods</data>. The kings from David’s <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132166\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">family line</data> were to be like David in those ways.</p><p>If they weren’t then the <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132326\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">covenant curses</data> would happen to all the Israelites. This included the curses from the <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132273\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">Mount Sinai</data> covenant and the temple being destroyed.</p><p>Both the people and the king had to obey God and worship only him. Only then would they be safe from their enemies and receive the covenant blessings.</p>",
